Here's a summary of everything that was built:

## ✅ What was built

**Project:** `SupportEmailTriage` — Cross-platform (Portable), VB.NET

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `Main.xaml` | Orchestrator: trigger → classify → route → (if critical) alert |
| `Workflows/ClassifyEmail.xaml` | Scores urgency by keyword + VIP sender detection |
| `Workflows/RouteEmail.xaml` | Forwards tagged email to support queue with triage header |
| `Workflows/AlertTeam.xaml` | Sends HTML escalation alert email to your team lead |

**How it works:**
- 🔔 **Trigger** — fires every time a new email lands in your M365 Inbox
- 🧠 **Classify** — scans subject + body for 18 urgency keywords (`urgent`, `outage`, `refund`, `legal`…) and checks sender against a VIP domain list → outputs `Critical`, `Priority`, or `Standard`
- 📤 **Route** — forwards to your support queue with a visible tag (`[CRITICAL [VIP]]`, `[PRIORITY]`, `[STANDARD]`) and a colour-coded triage banner
- 🚨 **Alert** (Critical only) — sends an immediate HTML alert email to your team lead with full email preview

