### Missing connections — setup required before running
Before you can debug or publish, you need to configure the two O365 connector nodes with a real connection. In UiPath Integration Service, create a **Microsoft Outlook 365** connection, then run:

```bash
cd /work/output/artifacts/SupportEmailTriage/SupportEmailTriage

# Configure the email trigger (replace UUIDs with your real values)
uip maestro flow node configure SupportEmailTriage.flow emailReceived1 \
  --detail '{"connectionId":"<YOUR_O365_CONNECTION_ID>","folderKey":"<YOUR_FOLDER_KEY>","eventMode":"polling"}' \
  --output json

# Configure the forward-email node
uip maestro flow node configure SupportEmailTriage.flow forwardToSupportQueue1 \
  --detail '{"connectionId":"<YOUR_O365_CONNECTION_ID>","folderKey":"<YOUR_FOLDER_KEY>","method":"POST","endpoint":"/forwardEmailV2","bodyParameters":{"messageId":"=js:$vars.emailReceived1.output.id","comment":"[PRIORITY TAG] Forwarded by SupportEmailTriage","toRecipients":["support-queue@yourcompany.com"]}}' \
  --output json

# Configure the alert email node
uip maestro flow node configure SupportEmailTriage.flow alertTeamLead1 \
  --detail '{"connectionId":"<YOUR_O365_CONNECTION_ID>","folderKey":"<YOUR_FOLDER_KEY>","method":"POST","endpoint":"/send-mail-v2","bodyParameters":{"subject":"=js:\"🚨 CRITICAL EMAIL ALERT: \" + $vars.emailReceived1.output.subject","toRecipients":["teamlead@yourcompany.com"],"body":"=js:\"A critical email was received from \" + $vars.emailReceived1.output.from.emailAddress.address"}}' \
  --output json
```

